	abstract = {A Mystery Braid is a craft object notable for its ability to be plaited without cutting the ends of the material. This thesis applies Artin’s presentation of the braid group to formalize the mathematical structure underlyingmystery braids. We develop an original notation system for describing braids on ribbons and modelling the construction of such braids using physical materials. Using this framework, we classify which mystery braids can be physically realised in craftwork, offering a mathematical understanding of braid structures with practical guidance for constructing mystery braids.},
